course: dictionary
lesson: 10657
title: Unkind words and actions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unkind means not kind. It describes saying or doing things that hurt or upset other people. Context helps you see this. In «Whispering unkind things behind someone's back is as bad as saying them out loud», the clue is that the words hurt someone who is not there to hear them.
explain: Unkind can describe actions as well as words. Calling names, leaving someone out and laughing at someone are all unkind. The word fits when you swap it into a sentence: «Leaving her out at lunch was unkind» still makes sense.
explain: Unkind is an adjective, so it can change its form. We say unkinder to compare two things, as in «Calling names is unkinder than sharing a joke», and unkindest for the most unkind thing. We can also say more unkind.
explain: Being kind is not always easy, but it is always the better choice. «Helping someone who is hurt is always right, even if that person has been unkind to you.» Kindness is still the right thing to do.
fact: Unkind means not kind, and it hurts or upsets other people.
fact: Unkind is an adjective: unkind, unkinder, unkindest, or more unkind.
fact: «Whispering unkind things behind someone's back is as bad as saying them out loud.»
fact: If someone is unkind to you, tell a trusted adult.
fact: Being unkind to animals is wrong too.
fact: «Helping someone who is hurt is always right, even if that person has been unkind to you.»
exercise: «Whispering unkind things behind someone's back is as bad as saying them out loud.» What does unkind mean here? | *Not kind, hurting or upsetting others | Loud and shouting | Funny and cheerful | Very quiet and gentle
exercise: Pick the word that makes the sentence right: Calling a friend names is ___ than sharing a joke. | unkindly | *unkinder | unkindest | kinder
exercise: «Helping someone who is hurt is always right, even if that person has been unkind to you.» What should you do when someone unkind is hurt? | Tell them they deserved it | Laugh at them | Ignore them and walk away forever | *Help them
test: Mia's classmate was unkind to her at lunch. What should she do? | Laugh along with the others | *Tell a trusted adult | Say nothing and be unkind back | Pretend it never happened
test: What does unkind describe? | *Saying or doing things that hurt others | Being very tall | Feeling sleepy after lunch | Running very fast
exam: «Being unkind to animals is wrong too.» Which meaning fits unkind best? | *Not kind, hurting or upsetting others | Very kind and generous | Lost and alone | Shy and quiet
